        "::: {.callout-important}\n",
        "## Task 1 — Sublayer/log-law crossover\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the code above as a starting point, find (numerically) the value of\n",
        "$y^+$ where the viscous-sublayer law and the log law intersect. Plot both\n",
        "laws, mark the intersection point, and briefly comment (2–3 sentences) on\n",
        "why neither law is accurate in the *buffer layer*.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.content-visible when-profile=\"solutions\"}\n",
        "::: {.solution-box}\n",
        "The intersection satisfies $y^+ = \\frac{1}{\\kappa}\\ln y^+ + B$, which gives\n",
        "$y^+ \\approx 11.1$ (e.g. via `scipy.optimize.brentq`). Neither law holds in\n",
        "the buffer layer ($5 \\lesssim y^+ \\lesssim 30$) because viscous and\n",
        "turbulent shear stresses are of comparable magnitude there — no single\n",
        "limiting balance applies."
      ],
      "id": "e0d448cb"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "from scipy.optimize import brentq\n",
        "yc = brentq(lambda y: y - (np.log(y) / kappa + B), 5, 30)\n",
        "print(f\"crossover at y+ = {yc:.2f}\")"
      ],
